Project Journal

2026-07-29 — Project Reframing and Domain Discovery

Background

This project began as an experiment in learning about artificial intelligence. I wanted to understand not only what AI could do, but how I could work alongside it effectively.

That experiment soon became practical.

I identified a recurring need at work: inventory data arrived in inconsistent spreadsheet formats and required repetitive cleanup before it could be used. Rather than simply asking AI to solve the problem, I began working with it to design and refine an ETL workflow that could automate the process.

The project gradually became more than an exercise in AI. It became an exploration of how human judgment and AI assistance can work together to solve a real problem.

Project Reframing

For the portfolio, the original workflow is being transformed into a fictional business system for Northstar Industrial Supply, a multi-warehouse industrial-parts distributor.

The goal is no longer simply to demonstrate that an ETL process works. The project is being developed as though it were a real client engagement, beginning with the business domain and moving deliberately toward requirements, data modeling, ETL, database design, and QA.

Current Direction

The project will eventually move through:

Business Domain → Requirements → Data → ETL → SQLite → QA

The emphasis is on understanding the problem before building the solution.

The spreadsheet is only the beginning. The larger goal is to demonstrate how I approach ambiguity, make decisions, use AI as a collaborative tool, and turn a practical problem into a thoughtful, testable Project Journal

